<task id="004" project="messaging-communication-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Schema: `sprk_communicationthread` entity + `sprk_thread` lookup + thread↔channel child table</title>
    <phase>W0 — Phase 0 Verification + Foundation</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>5</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>001</dependencies>
    <blocks>040, 050</blocks>
    <tags>dataverse, schema</tags>
    <rigor-hint>STANDARD</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Creates NEW Dataverse schema (entity + lookup + child table) — no BFF code, no Step 9.5 gates. STANDARD per §8 (new-file/new-surface creation with constraints). §11 Component Justification REQUIRED (a new entity is introduced).</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W0-B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-05</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Create the first-class communication thread data model (FR-05, design §6). Today there is NO thread entity — email "threading" is invisible pointer-chasing (`sprk_inreplyto` ancestry) and chat has no home at all (design §2). This task builds the thin, *queryable* grouping key that groups email reply-chains AND chat conversations channel-agnostically. Grouping key is LOCKED to option (A) per design §14.4.

    Create three schema artifacts via the `dataverse-create-schema` skill patterns:

    1. **`sprk_communicationthread` entity** (NEW) — kept deliberately THIN (design §6.1): a **topic** (text; derived from first message subject/participant label — no authoring UI in R1), an **anchor** via the **ADR-024 regarding family** (NOT a new regarding mechanism — reuse the existing polymorphic regarding lookups), a **thread-level privacy state** (the home for D-04 point-forward privacy), and a **participant set** representation. It is also the home for the ACS `ChatThreadId` (via the child table below).
    2. **`sprk_communication.sprk_thread` lookup** (NEW) — a lookup from every message to its thread. Direction-symmetric thread assignment (task 040) sets it on both inbound + outbound, all channels.
    3. **thread↔channel child table** (NEW, design D-03) — one row per `(thread, channel, external-ref)`. R1 populates the ACS `ChatThreadId`; email/SMS refs attach later with NO schema change ("channel is an attribute").

    Verify option-set integers (e.g., privacy-state choices) via Dataverse MCP before assignment, and consume task 001's schema-audit report so you add exactly what's missing (do not recreate existing columns). This is schema only — the thread-assignment LOGIC is task 040; the privacy ENFORCEMENT is task 042.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke Dataverse schema engineer. Fluent in the `dataverse-create-schema` skill (Web API + PowerShell for patterns PAC CLI can't do), the ADR-024 polymorphic regarding family, option-set integer conventions, and intersection/child-table modeling. You add exactly the schema the spec needs — nothing speculative.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `sprk_communicationthread` (thin: topic + ADR-024 anchor + privacy state + participants), the `sprk_communication.sprk_thread` lookup, and the thread↔channel child table exist in Dataverse (in the project solution), with verified option-set integers. A query "messages where `sprk_thread` = X" returns a conversation; the child table can hold the ACS `ChatThreadId`. Tasks 040 (resolver) and 050 (thread-read endpoint) can build against the real schema.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §6.1 rules out the alternatives and locks option (A): a JSON blob can't be filtered by Dataverse; leaning on *regarding* is the wrong dimension (a matter has many conversations). The thread entity gives thread-level privacy (D-04) and participants a real home; the child table makes "channel is an attribute" so SMS/email refs attach later with no schema change.

      §11 Component Justification (a NEW entity is introduced): (1) **Existing overlap** — none; grep/design §2 confirm no thread entity, no thread↔channel table, no `sprk_conversationid` grouping in use (task 001 verifies). (2) **Extension instead** — the lighter fallback (C: a `sprk_conversationid` field on `sprk_communication`) was considered and rejected in design §6.1 because thread-level privacy + participants would have no home; (A) is the locked choice. (3) **Concrete cost-of-doing-nothing** — without a queryable thread key, the timeline component (FR-10) and thread-read endpoint (FR-11) have nothing to filter on, and chat conversations have no grouping at all; "a matter shows a flat list of messages, not grouped threads" (design §2). This is a named contract failure (FR-05 acceptance: "every persisted message carries a `sprk_thread`; the child table holds the ACS thread id"), not "future flexibility."
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r1/notes/spikes/001-schema-audit.md (task 001 output — the confirmed column delta; consume it)</file>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r1/design.md (§6 threads, §6.1 grouping-key A, D-03 child table, §14.4)</file>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r1/spec.md (FR-05 + acceptance)</file>
      <file>docs/data-model/ (existing Dataverse entity schemas / ERD — for the regarding family + conventions)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">Thread anchor reuses the polymorphic regarding family — MUST NOT add a second regarding mechanism. Use the existing regarding lookups the association engine already writes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design §6.1 / §14.4">Grouping key is LOCKED to (A) `sprk_communicationthread` + `sprk_thread` lookup. Do NOT implement option C (`sprk_conversationid`) or option B (regarding+JSON).</constraint>
    <constraint source="design §6.1">Keep the entity THIN — topic, anchor, privacy state, participant set. No speculative columns; no topic-authoring UI schema.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design D-03">Thread↔channel child table = one row per `(thread, channel, external-ref)`; R1 populates ACS `ChatThreadId`; SMS/email refs attach later with no schema change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Verify all option-set integers via Dataverse MCP `describe`/`read_query` BEFORE assignment (privacy-state choice, channel-type on the child table). Consume task 001's audit — do not recreate existing columns.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-027">Author schema into the project's solution per managed-solution conventions; no direct prod-only unmanaged changes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Schema ONLY. No thread-assignment logic (that is 040), no privacy enforcement (that is 042), no BFF code.</constraint>
  </constraints>

