  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read task 001's `notes/spikes/001-schema-audit.md` + design §6.1/§14.4 + spec FR-05 to fix the exact schema to add (and confirm nothing already exists).</step>
    <step order="2">Via Dataverse MCP `describe`, re-confirm the ADR-024 regarding-family lookups available for the thread anchor and the `sprk_communicationtype` member set (for the child-table channel attribute).</step>
    <step order="3">Create the `sprk_communicationthread` entity (thin: topic text; ADR-024 regarding anchor; thread-level privacy-state choice — verify integers via MCP first; participant-set representation).</step>
    <step order="4">Create the `sprk_communication.sprk_thread` lookup (message → thread).</step>
    <step order="5">Create the thread↔channel child table: `(thread lookup, channel-type choice, external-ref text)`; ensure it can hold the ACS `ChatThreadId`; shape it so email/SMS refs attach later with no schema change.</step>
    <step order="6">Deploy the schema to the project solution (`dataverse-deploy` / skill patterns). Verify: a thread record can be created; a `sprk_communication` can point at it via `sprk_thread`; a child-table row holds an ACS `ChatThreadId`; a filter "`sprk_thread` = X" returns the messages.</step>
    <step order="7">Document the created schema (logical names, types, option-set integers, relationships) in the task notes / for the 081 architecture doc. Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (004 ✅) + `current-task.md`; confirm 040 + 050 unblocked.</step>
  </steps>

