  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`sprk_communicationthread` exists with: topic, an ADR-024 regarding-family anchor (no new mechanism), a thread-level privacy-state field, and a participant-set representation.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The `sprk_communication.sprk_thread` lookup exists (message → thread).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The thread↔channel child table exists, holds one row per `(thread, channel, external-ref)`, and can store the ACS `ChatThreadId`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A query "messages where `sprk_thread` = X" returns the conversation (verified against a test thread + message).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All option-set integers were verified via Dataverse MCP before assignment; no existing column was recreated (per the 001 audit).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No thread-assignment logic, no privacy enforcement, no BFF code was added (schema only).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Blocks 040 (`IThreadResolver` find-or-creates this entity + sets `sprk_thread`) and 050 (thread-read endpoint filters on `sprk_thread`). Depends on 001 (the schema-audit delta).

    Point-forward: historical emails have no thread and stay ungrouped until an optional backfill (deferred, out of R1 — design §6.5). Do not build backfill schema.

    Keep it thin. Design §6.1 explicitly warns against over-modeling: topic/anchor/privacy/participants only. The rich timeline is the component (060), not schema.
  </notes>

